Engine: a tactical battle reports its own screen id, and the gate the combat blocks are written under (open fix 52).

STATUS: APPLIED 30 September 2026 by work order 194 (Part B, the first of the
combat fixes reserved by work order 193) — orion2re 2495e1cf on
orionlayer-local (before: ab3f6892), this file's diff byte for byte (index lines
included). Required by tools/version_check.py since work order 194.

It was applied, from ~/orion2re on the orionlayer-local branch, with:

    patch -p1 < ~/orionlayerv3/doc/ext_combat_screen_id.patch

and a rebuild. It comes back off with `git revert 2495e1cf` or `patch -R -p1`,
and a rebuild.

WHAT IT IS FOR

    Nothing in cmbt*, comb* or combat* writes MOX::_current_screen, so a
    client saw 12 (SCREEN_MAIN_NEXT_TURN; 37 in a network game) for a whole
    battle and could not tell it from turn processing (work order 193,
    survey §3). ext::CombatGuard lives in COMBINIT::Tactical_Combat_ from
    just after Deploy_Ships_ to the end of the block that holds the turn
    loop, before End_Of_Combat_ writes the losses back: it reports 65, sets
    ext::g_combat_live — the gate every later combat block (53-57) is
    written under — and counts the battle in ext::g_combat_serial. The scan
    view (CMBTDRW1::Detailed_View_Ship_) reports 66 and the board popup
    (CMBTDRW1::Board_Popup_) 67 while a battle is live; the scan view is
    also opened from the fleet screen, the map and the Leaders screen, which
    keep their own ids.

    What is SENT changes, nothing the game reads: the override is the one
    ScreenOverride already used by open fixes 46, 49 and 50. An engine
    without OrionLayer behaves exactly as before. One marker, `OrionLayer,
    open fix 52.`, on one line at every changed place (ext_api.h,
    ext_api.cpp, combinit.cpp, cmbtdrw1.cpp).

